From: Win7 port restore
Subject: [PATCH] desktop: intranet mode switch, online-component hiding, and main-process gates

A single "Intranet Mode" switch turns the app into an air-gapped posture:
everything the app initiates outbound stops, while user-configured domains
(providers, proxies, local paths) are untouched. The switch lives on its
own settings page — pinned as the FIRST entry of the settings sidebar,
above Providers — so the air-gap master switch is one click away.

Settings & sync:
  - New page desktop/src/pages/settings/IntranetModeSettings.tsx hosts the
    switch (promoted out of GeneralSettings, which stays untouched);
    Settings.tsx gains an "intranetMode" rail tab above Providers.
  - UserSettings.intranetMode + settingsStore.setIntranetMode() with
    optimistic update and rollback; hydrated from GET /api/settings/user.
  - The server broadcasts network_policy_changed on every toggle; chatStore
    mirrors the authoritative value into settingsStore, so every open
    window (and other clients) re-renders immediately — no restart.

UI hiding (first gate, cosmetic only; the main process still enforces):
  - About: update card (check/proxy/release notes) and GitHub/social links.
  - Sidebar: skill-market entry. An already-open market tab shows an
    "unavailable under intranet mode" notice and stops issuing requests.
  - Settings rail: the IM Adapters ("IM 接入") tab hides — external IM
    channels are unreachable in an air-gapped deployment; if the page is
    active when the switch flips, Settings falls back to the intranet
    page. Adapter configs themselves are left intact on disk.
  - Computer Use: only the "Download Python 3" external-link button hides
    (the offline bundle ships Python); status checks and path config stay.
  - Update store never enters the checking state.
  - Provider form modal (add/edit provider): the preset "Get API Key"
    button and the preset promo strip hide — both are pure online entry
    points (external links to SaaS consoles). The modal itself stays:
    adding intranet/self-hosted providers is THE air-gap use case.
  - General settings → WebSearch: the Tavily/Brave "Get API Key" links
    hide (WebSearch itself is force-disabled server-side by patch 014).
  - About: the two GitHub repo cards (upstream + this fork) STAY visible
    under intranet mode — they are attribution/source information, not
    functional online entries; intranet mode blocks network behaviour,
    it does not hide information. Clicking them is a no-op via the
    openUrl() short-circuit; hover styling is unchanged.

Focus hydration (broadcast edge case):
  - The network_policy_changed broadcast rides per-session WebSockets, so
    a freshly restarted app with no open session missed remote flips and
    needed a page reload. settingsStore now re-pulls GET /api/settings/user
    on window focus / visibilitychange→visible (500 ms debounce): the two
    paths share userSettingsPatch() so full loads and hydration write the
    same shape. api/settings.ts stamps every PUT; hydration skips when a
    save is still in flight (<1 s) so the optimistic UI is never clobbered
    by a stale server read.

Main-process gates (authoritative, uncached settings read per call):
  - electron/services/intranetMode.ts reads intranetMode from
    <CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR>/settings.json — the same file the server writes;
    the reader lives in the desktop project because the electron bundle
    cannot import server sources.
  - electron/services/intranetNetworkGuard.ts (new): Chromium's own
    background networking (spell-check dictionary downloads, component
    updater) is disabled/pinned to a loopback sink — observed as SYN_SENT
    from the NetworkService process, entirely independent of app code.
    main.ts installs the guard.
  - electron/services/systemProxyBridge.ts: under intranet mode the
    bridge only forwards to loopback / RFC1918 / ULA / link-local
    destinations (DNS-resolved and checked), so CLI children tunnelling
    through the bridge can never open a socket to the public internet.
  - uiStore.ts: 'intranetMode' joins SettingsTab (the rail tab type).
  - shell.ts openExternalUrl(): http(s) targets are refused before the
    electron module even loads (choke point for IPC + setWindowOpenHandler);
    mailto / system-settings schemes survive.
  - updater.ts checkForUpdates(): returns null without touching
    electron-updater and drops any pending update, so a later download
    has nothing to act on.

Locales: en / zh / zh-TW / jp / kr.


